@startuml vdso
'
' Engineered by  Christian Schnapka
'                Embedded Principal+ Engineer
'                Macstab GmbH · Hamburg, Germany
'                https://macstab.com
'
' clock_gettime(2) dispatch with libchaos-time.so preloaded.
'
' Key fact: libc calls the vDSO INSIDE its own clock_gettime, downstream
' of the wrapper, so the wrapper decides before and mutates after.
' The libraries' own clocks (rule-file throttle, @from/@until) call the
' vDSO directly and are therefore outside libchaos-time's reach.
'
' Reference: docs/PLATFORM.md §5, docs/TIME.md §2 and §10
'            src/time/chaos_time_hooks.c, src/common/chaos_clock.h
'            vdso(7) Linux man-pages
'
title clock_gettime dispatch with libchaos-time.so preloaded

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 4
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor                 #2C3E50
  LifeLineBorderColor        #2C3E50
  LifeLineBackgroundColor    #ECF0F1
  ParticipantBorderColor     #2C3E50
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantFontStyle       bold
  GroupBackgroundColor       #FDFEFE
  GroupBorderColor           #95A5A6
}
hide footbox

participant App
participant "libchaos-time.so" as Wrapper
participant "libc"             as Glibc
participant "kernel vDSO"      as Vdso
participant "kernel syscall"   as Kernel

note over Vdso
  x86_64:  __vdso_clock_gettime   (TSC / pvclock)
  aarch64: __kernel_clock_gettime (CNTVCT_EL0)
end note

App     ->  Wrapper : clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts)
note right of Wrapper
  guard set or ts == NULL: straight to the
  real function. gettimeofday, time and
  timespec_get(TIME_UTC) take the same path
  as a CLOCK_REALTIME read.
end note
Wrapper ->  Vdso    : config refresh: throttle clock\n(chaos_clock.h, direct vDSO call, CLOCK_MONOTONIC)
Wrapper ->  Wrapper : LATENCY rule? sleep via real usleep/nanosleep\nERRNO rule? (each effect: own lookup, own decision)

alt ERRNO fires
    Wrapper --> App : -1, errno set
else Passthrough to real
    Wrapper ->  Glibc  : real clock_gettime(...) under the guard\n(raw SYS_clock_gettime while unresolved)
    alt clock served by the vDSO
        Glibc -> Vdso   : __vdso_clock_gettime / __kernel_clock_gettime
        Vdso  --> Glibc : ts
    else CPUTIME clocks, or no usable vDSO clocksource
        Glibc -> Kernel : SYS_clock_gettime
        Kernel --> Glibc: ts
    end
    Glibc   --> Wrapper : 0, ts
    Wrapper ->  Wrapper : maybe OFFSET, then REGRESS\n(post-call mutation of the returned value only)
    Wrapper --> App     : 0, possibly mutated ts
end

note across
  Bypass cases — wrapper NOT invoked (docs/TIME.md §10):
  • Code issues syscall(SYS_clock_gettime, ...) itself.
  • Code locates the vDSO itself (AT_SYSINFO_EHDR) and calls it: the Go runtime does,
    with or without cgo.
  • Calls libc makes to its own functions internally (pthread_cond_timedwait timeouts, ...).
  • Statically linked binary (no dynamic loader, no LD_PRELOAD).
end note

@enduml
